{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWYWmoEpRYKDDVwwk2Uv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013knjMzWR1MG2ayUs1srJPx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: axios ReDoS (CVE-2021-3749)\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n- **CVE**: [CVE-2021-3749](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-3749)\n- **Affected package**: `axios` (npm)\n- **Vulnerability type**: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity (ReDoS) in the `trim()` helper used while parsing response headers, exploitable via a crafted header value.\n- **Vulnerable code path** (present in this workspace's vendored copy of axios): `/workspace/axios/lib/utils.js:189-191` (`trim()`), invoked from `/workspace/axios/lib/helpers/parseHeaders.js:37-38`.\n- **Affected version range**: `< 0.21.2`\n- **Fixed version**: `0.21.2` (and all subsequent releases, including the `0.26.x`/`0.27.x` line used in this workspace)\n\n`/workspace/axios` itself is a standalone mirror of the upstream `axios` project checked out at tag `v0.21.1` (confirmed via `package.json` and the local git log: \"Mirror of axios/axios at v0.21.1\"). It is **not** consumed as a dependency by any other repo in this workspace (no `file:`/`link:`/`workspace:` reference to it was found in any manifest or lockfile) — it exists only as a reference copy of the vulnerable source, not a live dependent.\n\n## 2. Direct Dependents\n\nTwo manifests declare a direct dependency on `axios`:\n\n| Repo | Manifest | Declared range |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grafana | `/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json:73` | `axios: ^0.26.1` |\n| Druid (web console) | `/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71` | `axios: ^0.26.1` |\n\nNo other `package.json` in the workspace declares `axios` directly (checked all manifests under `/workspace/grafana` and `/workspace/druid`, including `/workspace/druid/website/package.json`, which has no axios dependency).\n\n## 3. Transitive Paths\n\n### Grafana\n\nGrafana is a Yarn (Berry/PnP-style) monorepo with a single root lockfile: `/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock`. Two independent resolutions of `axios` exist in that lockfile, from two separate requirers:\n\n1. **Direct** — `grafana-toolkit` (`/workspace/grafana/packages/grafana-toolkit/package.json:73`) requires `^0.26.1` → resolves to **axios 0.26.1** (`/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12397-12403`), with its own transitive dep `follow-redirects: ^1.14.8`.\n2. **Transitive** — the root `/workspace/grafana/package.json:246` devDependency `wait-on: 7.0.1` requires `axios: ^0.27.2` (`/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock` `wait-on@npm:7.0.1` block, ~line 36864) → resolves to **axios 0.27.2** (`/workspace/grafana/yarn.lock:12406-12412`), with transitive deps `follow-redirects: ^1.14.9` and `form-data: ^4.0.0`.\n\nThere is no evidence the Grafana plugin SDK vendors its own copy of axios — `grafana-toolkit` (which is part of the plugin-build tooling) pulls axios in as a plain npm dependency resolved through the standard Yarn lockfile, not a vendored/bundled copy.\n\n### Druid\n\nThe Druid web console is a separate, self-contained npm project with its own lockfile: `/workspace/druid/web-console/package-lock.json`. It declares `axios: ^0.26.1` directly (`/workspace/druid/web-console/package.json:71`), which resolves to a single entry:\n\n- **axios 0.26.1** (`/workspace/druid/web-console/package-lock.json:30883-30888`), with transitive dependency `follow-redirects: ^1.14.8`.\n\nNo other axios resolution exists in this lockfile — it is a single, direct, non-transitive dependency for the web console.\n\n## 4. Version Analysis — Are We Vulnerable?\n\n| Repo | Resolved axios version(s) | Vulnerable to CVE-2021-3749 (`< 0.21.2`)? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grafana — `grafana-toolkit` | 0.26.1 | **No** — patched |\n| Grafana — `wait-on` (transitive, root devDependency) | 0.27.2 | **No** — patched |\n| Druid — `web-console` | 0.26.1 | **No** — patched |\n| `/workspace/axios` (standalone mirror, not a dependent) | 0.21.1 | Yes, but unused/unreferenced by any dependency graph in this workspace |\n\n**Conclusion**: All live dependents in the workspace (Grafana's `grafana-toolkit` and root `wait-on` devDependency, and Druid's `web-console`) already resolve to patched axios versions (0.26.1 / 0.27.2), both well above the fixed version 0.21.2. **No actual blast radius exists in the current lockfile state** — the vulnerable 0.21.1 code only exists as an unreferenced standalone mirror at `/workspace/axios` and is not pulled into any build. No remediation/patching action is required for Grafana or Druid based on current resolved dependency versions; the only recommended follow-up is to confirm no other environment (e.g., a build/CI cache or an unpinned range) resolves an older axios version than what is captured in these lockfiles.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41875,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0bb588e-4294-4b01-9b66-d3f898a77e33","uuid":"9c6b0f8d-cf5a-40e6-9a1e-c4ed60834842","timestamp":"2026-07-29T14:57:18.281Z","request_id":"req_011CdWYWk3KWJiTRpj4VFVmU"}
